WEBVTT

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.480
Excuse me for dropping in 
when you're having so much fun, but...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.570
Is the old man 
Dr. Taklamakan Strangelove here?

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.440
If he doesn't come out, 
I'm just going to have to...

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.530
Hold it. It is I. I am Dr. Love.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.330
Just how many body doubles do you
 think I've caught up until now?

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:37.010
I can tell if you're the real one 
or not with my SPH.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.560
<b>Something to Believe in: Part 1</b>

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.730
How long are you going to play dumb?

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.750
I don't know.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.690
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:19.120
Don't be ridiculous!

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.070
This is footage taken right before 
your pursuit of Dragline, who escaped.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:28.160
We have footage of you cutting through 
the grid at the detention center,

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.580
and letting him escape 
captured with a special camera.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.750
You can't talk your way out of this.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.960
What are you plotting?

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.380
I...

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:40.960
I don't know... I...

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:43.730
We're not going to fall for that!

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.800
She really has lost consciousness.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.010
What are the results of the lie-detector SPH?

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.380
We were unable to detect anything.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.600
She is a spy!

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.820
We'll make her confess, no matter what.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.760
Next, head to Interrogation Room 6.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:04.400
We're not even done fixing up <i>Jeanrenoi-R</i> 
from the DeMille attack yet.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.730
This is the last thing we need.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:09.990
It can't be helped. Sonokata's a suspect.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.790
She's a suspect but the footage 
of her letting a murderer escape

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.040
was captured with 
a special camera, right?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.660
Of course she's a spy.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.690
Misuzu hasn't confessed, chu.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.200
Well it's still true that there's footage of it.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.860
Misuzu might have been 
looking into all of us, too.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.310
That's not true, chu!

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.170
I've been with Misuzu ever since 
she joined the bureau, so I know, chu!

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:31.480
Both the way you think 
and your SPH reeks of a kid.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.930
And you reek just as bad as your afro!

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.390
And that's enough.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.690
Do you think that Misuzu is a spy, Chuta?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.660
Of course not.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.600
Even though she was caught on camera?

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:53.030
Even then, I trust Sonokata. Um... for the
 same reason as Assistant Inspector Chips.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:56.910
But unlike Chips, you haven't 
known Misuzu for very long.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:01.380
Wha— W-Well, yeah, but... 
you seem rather persistent about this.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.680
Do you want to make Sonokata the culprit?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.140
No! I just want to know 
why you want to trust Sonokata,

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.970
even when it means averting 
your eyes from the truth.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:12.900
I'm not averting my eyes from the truth...

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.400
Next. Come into the interrogation room.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.430
Yes, sir.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.930
In regards to the fever that the suspect 
has developed for the past two hours,

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.510
the cause of it is still unknown.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.890
Fix it! Straighten her up!

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:39.210
What do you want? Investigator Belalugo is busy.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.560
Then I'll just wait right here.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.500
If words aren't enough...

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.380
Ow!

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.340
Wh-Why, you...

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.850
I guess I don't have a choice.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:03.590
Jeez, you're hard...

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.820
Laine Brick!

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:13.650
One of your subordinates tried to get rid of me 
with violence, so I used self-defense.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:19.060
If you doubt me, check the special 
camera footage that you like so much.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.710
What do you want?

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:25.210
As the chief of this bureau, I request an 
interview with Officer Misuzu Sonokata.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:28.670
Request denied! I have 
no obligation to let you see her.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:33.600
Misuzu should have a 
high fever right about now.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.930
And if a suspect becomes
 ill during interrogation,

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:40.610
they should be able to accept treatment 
from their personal physician.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.970
Personal physician?

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:48.010
That's only reserved for special cases 
for those ill who are above Level 50.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:52.370
Yes... and she falls in that case.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:56.650
If I told you that she's a test subject of the
 Taklamakan Project, you should understand.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:57.910
What?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.930
You'll allow me to send her personal physician 
and an assistant to treat her, won't you?

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.540
Very well.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:09.170
However, I won't be going any easier 
on the interrogation!

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:13.630
Chief!

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.060
There's an emergency message 
from Superintendent Kieshi.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.150
All right. I'll be right there.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:26.740
So that's the only conversation that you had 
with Officer Sonokata at the detention center?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:27.810
Yes...

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.940
And everything you said is the truth?

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.630
<i>Again with the truth thing.</i>

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:36.790
<i>Jeez... everyone going on about truths.</i>

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:39.430
Officer Kokonose, was that the truth?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.660
<i>Even Dolugh said I was bending 
the truth earlier...</i>

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:41.950
Chuta, he's asking you a question.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.740
Oh... uh...

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.190
Look into my eyes!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.120
Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.630
Next.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.880
Chuta, were you thinking 
about something earlier?

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:02.500
This is all because you asked me why
 I trust Sonokata before I got interrogated.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:06.500
Ow.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:07.780
Ow!

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.980
What do you think you're doing? 
You're going to crush my horn.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:14.550
Horn? Y-You're the one who bumped into me.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:17.970
I don't remember. I was out of it 
from just waking up.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.070
<i>What? She's making it sound like my fault!</i>

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.620
Sorry. She's suffering from jetlag.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.740
Are you all right?

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.790
I-I'm fine. Thanks...

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:37.220
<i>They look to be around my age...</i>

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.510
Chuta!

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:40.000
Do you have a second?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.240
Yes.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:46.810
This is...

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:55.590
<i>I still don't believe that Sonokata 
let Dragline escape back then.</i>

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.460
Hurry and run...

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:00.460
Sonokata!

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:03.950
This isn't good. Her memories 
are starting to get muddled.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.750
Hang in there, Misuzu.

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:09.750
Wh-What's going on? 
What did they do to Sonokata?

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:11.640
They didn't do anything to her.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:13.970
Her medicine lost its effect.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.330
Medicine?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.350
Do you remember me telling you 
that Misuzu was taking medicine

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.850
to let her adapt to the environment?

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:25.060
It's the medicine she got from sick bay.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:32.800
Misuzu doesn't know it, but it's a drug to help 
the aftereffects from a top-secret project.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.990
Aftereffects?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:34.780
Yes.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:41.680
What I'm about to tell you is a secret 
that only the chief, Chips, and I know.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:47.810
Misuzu was forced to undergo 
a certain treatment in the past.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:50.630
But because of that, 
her body's balance was destroyed

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:53.280
and she lost a half year's worth 
of her memories.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.040
What?

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:59.790
That treatment implanted an SPH-producing 
organ within her from another individual,

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.220
and her personality underwent a change.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.720
It's called the Taklamakan Project.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.690
But the project ended in failure,

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.980
and most of those who 
underwent the procedure

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.800
lost their lives, or their bodies 
ended up with some defect.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:15.970
And...

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.910
Misuzu lost all of her memories 
regarding the treatment,

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:23.790
and she became unable to survive 
without taking the medication.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.370
Why was Sonokata forced 
to undergo something like that?

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:30.190
I don't have the answer to that. 
It's top secret.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:32.990
Why did you tell me this?

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:34.250
Why else?

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:38.390
It's because you're in a 
position to protect Misuzu.

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:43.850
Protect Sonokata... Me?

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:49.850
By the way, the chief knows 
that I was going to talk to you about this.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:51.070
The chief...

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:54.440
Investigations department 2nd Division, 
you have a mission.

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:56.140
Come to the chief's quarters.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:01.820
I need you to bring this scientist, who is 
currently residing on Earth, to the bureau.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:06.200
Dr. Love. He's one of the best 
scientists in the universe.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.880
He's an old acquaintance of mine. 
He's 500 years old and a weirdo.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.160
500 years old?!

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:14.870
Dr. Love hates interferences,

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:17.210
so we came this far without 
providing him with security.

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:20.920
But four out of five of his body doubles 
have been killed lately.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:21.930
Ack!

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:24.560
Since it's become this dangerous,

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:26.430
we aren't able to leave this matter alone.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.700
ēlDLIVE HQ has sent an order 
to provide protection.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:31.820
Um, but...

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:33.680
Right now, I'm worried about Misuzu, chu.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.060
Are you worried, too, Chuta?

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:38.560
Yes.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.700
Don't let your personal feelings 
get in the way of your work!

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.070
I-I'm sorry!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.600
Well, I understand how you feel.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.840
Ever since Misuzu was arrested,

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.610
I've eaten way too many dumplings.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.470
And this is completely coincidental...

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:57.540
But this mission might end up
 being a way to save Misuzu.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:02.600
I see. Dr. Love's full name is...

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.770
Taklamakan Strangelove...

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:09.590
He's the one who came up with 
this Taklamakan Project.

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:13.010
What does that have to do 
with saving Misuzu?

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:17.190
The Doctor and I think that the actions 
that led to Misuzu being suspected of spying

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:21.050
are due to a side effect of the
 medicine that she's taking.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:21.900
What?

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:26.290
It's unconfirmed, but a similar incident
 has been reported in the past.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:31.410
Those who have taken this medicine apparently 
have done things that they don't remember.

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:35.480
If we can get Dr. Love, 
who created the medicine,

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:38.710
to testify that Misuzu cutting through 
the grid was a side effect,

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.120
this whole thing will be deemed an accident, 
and she'll be declared innocent.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.800
I see.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.560
I didn't understand all of that...

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:45.630
I understood.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:49.050
...but if we bring Dr. Love back, 
Sonokata will be saved, right?

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:50.920
You'll go, won't you?

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.550
Yoyosa!

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:55.980
You'll be working with the 5th Division 
on this mission.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:58.850
I've given the details to the leader 
of the 5th Division.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:01.200
We were transferred upside down.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:02.130
He did it again.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:03.850
Come on, Sheronimo!

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.980
But I'm in a good mood, 
so I'll let him off the hook, chu.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:11.100
Because if we bring Dr. Love back, 
Misuzu will be declared innocent, chu!

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:15.070
True. See, Dolugh? I was right, wasn't I?

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:17.490
I told you that Sonokata wasn't a spy.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:20.080
I never said she was.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:20.910
Huh?

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:25.210
I just wanted to know why you trusted Misuzu 
when you didn't have anything to back it up.

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:27.260
Are you still talking about that?

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.800
I want to be included 
in this conversation, too!

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:32.510
I can't hear the Monitalien's voice, chu!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.050
Freeze!

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:36.810
Likewise.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.720
Whoa, wh-what?

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:40.780
Oh, it's you guys.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:41.470
Huh?

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:44.830
Pardon our rudeness, Assistant Inspector Chips.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:46.960
You guys!

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:50.260
We've been waiting for you.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:52.520
We're from ēlDLIVE investigations 
department Division 5,

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.510
and we'll be joining you on this mission.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:05.970
<b>Veronica Borowczyk</b>

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.690
Talk about calculating.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:12.300
Still...

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:13.420
What's matter?

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:16.900
Misuzu's arrest and Dr. Love's guarding...

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:19.680
The timing feels too convenient.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.180
Oh, you're the girl I ran into 
after the interrogation!

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:25.560
That was my bad.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:29.280
There, I apologized! Now it's your turn!

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:30.160
What?!

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:33.960
Let me introduce you, chu. 
This is the 5th Division's—

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:38.110
Assistant Inspector Veronica Borowczyk, 
leader of the 5th Division.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.870
And this is—

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:43.830
Officer Nina Mikhailovna Pavlova.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.950
Call me Ninotchka.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:46.840
There you have it, chu!

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.340
Oh, I'm...

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.210
Officer Chuta Kokonose, right?

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:57.130
The so-called super rookie who arrested 
a C-ranked criminal in his entrance exam.

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:00.190
You're famous, Chuta.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.270
Wow, so cute!

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:05.820
Are you the Monitalien 
everyone's talking about?

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:10.300
Wh-What's wrong, Dolugh?

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:13.090
That's the first time 
a stranger has touched me!

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:15.450
U-Uh, I'm sorry.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:17.570
Still, you know,

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:21.450
you seem to be every bit as
 boring a guy as the rumors say.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.450
There are rumors?

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:25.030
What are you saying?!

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.700
Just what's on my mind.

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:30.380
She's a nice person deep down.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:33.480
She just speaks her mind a little too freely.

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:36.280
I don't think of you as boring.

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:39.470
Right. You're into frail boys like him.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:41.260
V-Veronica!

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:41.690
Frail...?

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:44.690
Seriously, though, 
what has Misuzu gone and done?

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.610
It's so dumb, it's not even funny.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:50.320
Oh, this is her unique way 
of showing her love.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:54.190
The three of us entered ēlDLIVE 
at the same time,

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:57.080
and we're close enough to 
really let one another have it.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:00.450
If Misuzu and I really let each other have it, 
we'd be fighting to the death.

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.460
<i>Contemporaries, huh?</i>

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.470
All right. Let's get to work.

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:11.210
If we work together, I'll be able to tell 
at once if you really are a super rookie.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.980
Okay, here we go!

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.170
Yeah!

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:21.270
We're supposed to make contact 
with Dr. Love in that restaurant,

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:25.090
but keep your guards up, because 
there might be people out for him.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.390
Go inside and check things out, 
Officer Kokonose.

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:30.850
Yoyosa!

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:43.420
You're being too conspicuous!

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:46.560
Can't you use your Monitalien 
to peek inside or something?!

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:47.780
There's an idea.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:51.590
Though most people use one of these.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.590
Okay, all clear.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:57.930
We are a go.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:01.340
<i>You could've just done this yourself 
from the start, you demon!</i>

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:02.980
Are you all right?

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:06.020
You can use my handkerchief, if you like.

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:09.860
Thanks, but I have my own.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:13.520
Wow, it's nice and ironed.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.030
Must've been your mother, right?

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:16.480
Nah, it was me.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:19.300
That's amazing!

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:23.540
<i>By contrast, she's an angel!</i>

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.830
<i>Next up, we have a story from overseas.</i>

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:29.050
<i>An Italian man...</i>

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.360
Quit gawking.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:31.570
Dr. Love isn't here.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:36.060
Did you really think he'd be casually 
sipping a cuppa when his life is in danger?

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:37.620
He'd obviously send someone.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:39.260
Welcome.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.350
Table for three?

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:48.770
Sorry! My grandpa forgot his hat here!

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:51.030
Ah, I see.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.870
You're one of those customers.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:55.150
<i>Grandpa?</i>

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:57.970
I get it. That was a secret code, Chuta.

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:01.160
Like, "What's the magic word?"

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:06.290
If only you'd come sooner, 
things wouldn't have come to this.

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.340
Is he dead?

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:13.370
What's the meaning of this?

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:16.370
I welcome you, ēlDLIVE.

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:22.340
If you're here, that means 
the real Dr. Love should be nearby.

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.940
So you're the one who killed his body doubles!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:29.340
Assistant Officer Chips, 
contact the <i>Jeanrenoi-R!</i>

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.560
You got it, chu.

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:31.640
Slow down.

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:35.110
SPH comms won't work in here.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.610
You can't talk to your friends.

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:42.240
Now, it's my turn to ask the questions.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:47.330
You know where Dr. Love is, don't you?

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.040
This is bad, Chuta! We're surrounded!

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:51.620
Very well.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:54.050
If it's a fight you want, 
a fight you will get!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.330
SPH...

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:10.900
<i>Kick</i>

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:10.900
Kopnięcie!

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:12.310
Fire!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.690
SPH...

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:19.690
Obrót akcja!

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:19.690
<i>Spin action!</i>

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:22.400
Okay!

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:24.590
That's ēlDLIVE for you.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:29.310
But what if they were innocent civilians?

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.080
What was I doing?

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:33.310
Where am I?

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:34.670
I thought I was...

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.260
Were these people...

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:38.670
...hypnotized?

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:40.030
Also...

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:46.880
If that detonates, this whole 
restaurant will be blown to pieces.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:53.940
Now, where is Dr. Love?

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.070
We don't know.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:59.650
If you don't answer me honestly, 
everyone here goes boom.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:01.740
Veronica.

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:04.950
He's underground, beneath this restaurant.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.400
That's all I know!

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:07.810
I see.

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:09.250
Down here, huh?

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:12.660
Then I guess I'd better blow up 
this place, after all.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:16.460
Adiós, ladies and gentlemen.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:21.060
Hurry up and stop the bomb!

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:22.860
But how?

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:24.220
Ice, Chuta!

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:28.810
I saw a bomb squad freeze one 
on TV while you were asleep!

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:30.700
Who said you could do that?

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:32.470
There's no time, Chuta.

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:35.970
Okay, the same move as 
that time we froze the gum off?

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.060
Sympathy!

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:40.270
Freezing Bomb Stop!

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:47.430
Okay, that delayed the explosion a little!

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:50.170
Get behind me, everyone!

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:51.450
Ninotchka.

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:52.710
I know.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:09.090
Everyone's okay, chu.

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.870
All of you, hurry up and head somewhere safe!

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:17.790
Was that your SPH just now?

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.520
Y-Yes.

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:24.490
It was really, uh, incredible!

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:26.320
U-Um...

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:28.940
Did you see?

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:32.360
N-No, um...

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.420
Hey, Officer Kokonose!

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:36.950
This is all your fault!

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.680
If you'd frozen the bomb right at the start,

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:42.960
he wouldn't have found out 
where Dr. Love was,

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:45.370
and this place wouldn't have been blown up!

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:49.470
My conclusion: you're no super rookie.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:51.000
You're dead weight.

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:53.290
Dead weight...?

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:54.730
That hurts me, too.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:56.820
That's going too far, Veronica.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.720
He won't get it unless I spell it out.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.300
Dead weight...

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:03.270
Oh no! Chuta's confidence 
is vanishing into the ether!

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.970
So you're all set to escape, huh?

00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:09.770
It's him!

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:12.750
I finally get to meet the real deal!

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:17.150
No!

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:29.640
How awful!

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:33.390
How noisy.

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:34.880
Someone's there!

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.480
Do you need this geezer for something?

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:53.760
You're too late, though.

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:27.360
Oh, Assistant Inspector Veronica.

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:29.600
What do I do? I ruined my bed again.

00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:30.980
Wait, you wet your bed?

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:32.060
As if!

00:23:32.060 --> 00:23:34.790
My horn tore a hole in it 
when I turned over in my sleep!

00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:36.010
Next time on <i>ēlDLIVE,</i>

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.270
"Something to Believe in: Part 2."

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Next Time
Something to Believe in: Part 2</b>

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:39.840
Talk about misleading!
